# L §6.1: "A model is one or more .tally files in one directory tree"; "use a = "file" sha256 "…"" imports a closed
# model; E §3.1 step 1: its hash is of "its canonical text, its files reprinted and taken in the order of their paths
# in its directory tree", every file (the scenario file included: "A reality's hash covers every file", L §6.1). The
# member a is the tree ../A: its law part holds the rate (0.12) its model reads; its ask q is asked as a.q (L §6.1);
# its scenario file is no part of its base (L §6.4 "The base is whole without its scenarios").
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A" sha256 "e6d5403b51fe7411ad65011b8b940d26098814144cccb5cfa52220ced833dfd6"

ask r: a.rate
=== A/reality.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def doubled: num = rate + rate
=== A/law/pit.tally
part pit
  tally 2
  law

source act "ustawa"

input rate: num

version pit_2026
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "art. 1"
=== A/asks/q.tally
part asks
  tally 2

ask q: doubled
=== A/scenarios/s.tally
scenario s over ana
  tally 2
  from 2026-06-01

version s_rate
  cite act
  governs 2026-06-01..
  known 2025-01-01
  replace rate = 0.5 "scenariusz"
=== expect r a.q
r: 0.12
  cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 0.24
  cut 2026-10-20
